  "solution": {
    "text": "Kieselguhr, an amorphous form of silica is used in filtration plants. <br/>Quartz is one of the most common minerals in the earth’s crust having a specific crystalline form. <br/>Cristobalite is a high temperature polymorph of silica, having same chemical formula as quartz but distinct crystal structure. <br/>Tridymite is also a high temperature polymorph of silica and occurs as hexagonal crystals.",
